      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    prices = [\n        120, 122, 121, 124, 125, 127, 126, 129, 130, 128,\n        131, 132, 134, 135, 137, 136, 138, 139, 140, 142,\n        141, 143, 144, 146, 145\n    ]\n    period_ema = 10\n    period_atr = 10\n    multiplier = 1.5\n\n    # The provided Keltner Channel method treats each price change as\n    # the true range, using Wilder smoothing for the ATR.\n    ema = sum(prices[:period_ema]) / period_ema\n    smoothing_factor = 2 / (period_ema + 1)\n    for price in prices[period_ema:]:\n        ema = (price - ema) * smoothing_factor + ema\n\n    true_ranges = [\n        abs(current - previous)\n        for previous, current in zip(prices[:-1], prices[1:])\n    ]\n    atr = sum(true_ranges[:period_atr]) / period_atr\n    for true_range in true_ranges[period_atr:]:\n        atr = (atr * (period_atr - 1) + true_range) / period_atr\n\n    answer = round(ema + multiplier * atr, 2)\n    return answer\n```",
